# Build context exclusions for every root-context image (users, orders,
# email-preview, web). The context is the REPO ROOT for all of them, and the
# whole tree is uploaded to the Docker daemon BEFORE the first instruction runs
# — so anything not excluded here is paid for on every build, whether or not a
# COPY ever names it.
#
# That cost was 7.0G before this file existed: 4.9G of Terraform provider
# caches under infra/**/.terraform plus 1.5G of node_modules. No Dockerfile in
# this repo copies either — each one COPYs narrow, explicit paths (manifests,
# src/, proto/, prisma/, emails/) — so the entire upload was pure waste.
#
# RULE: exclusions here are BROAD, and each Dockerfile re-includes what it
# needs by naming it in a COPY. Adding a path below cannot silently break a
# build that does not reference it; check the COPY lines before excluding
# something a Dockerfile does name.

# ── Dependencies (reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile) ────────────
# pnpm installs from pnpm-lock.yaml in the deps stage; a host node_modules is
# both useless (wrong platform — macOS binaries in a Linux image) and huge.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# ── Terraform provider caches (4.9G) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Downloaded per-module by `terraform init`. Nothing in any image reads them.
**/.terraform
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*

# ── Build outputs (regenerated inside the image) ────────────────────────────
# Copying a host dist/ in would let a developer's stale local build silently
# become the image's contents — the same class of bug the users Dockerfile
# guards against by regenerating its Prisma client after COPY.
dist
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj
apps/web/.angular
services/*/src/generated

# ── Python tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv
.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__

# ── VCS & CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.github
.gitignore

# ── Secrets — belt and braces ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are gitignored too, but a build context is not a git checkout: an
# untracked .env.local.users sitting in the working tree would otherwise be
# uploaded and, if any COPY caught it, baked into a layer. The committed
# .env.example contract is not secret, so it stays.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Editor / agent / docs material, never served or compiled ────────────────
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.cursor
.windsurf
.ai
.superpowers
.obsidian
docs
spike

# apps/web/design/exports holds 56 static HTML design references — reference
# material for humans, never served by the web image (nginx serves only
# dist/web/browser). Excluded explicitly because "design" reads like source.
apps/web/design

# ── Test artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
e2e/test-results
e2e/screenshots
coverage

# ── OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
